{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ROM",
  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What shall we say then? Shall we continue in sin, that grace may abound?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By no means: how shall we, that are dead to sin, live any longer therein?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Know ye not, that so many of us as were baptized into Jesus Christ, were baptized into his death?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore we are buried with him by baptism into death: that as Christ was raised from the dead by the glory of the Father, even so we also should walk in newness of life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if we have been planted together in the likeness of his death, we shall be also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the likeness",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " resurrection:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowing this, that our old man is crucified with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that the body of sin may be destroyed, that henceforth we should not serve sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he that is dead is freed from sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now if we are dead with Christ, we believe that we shall also live with him:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowing that Christ, being raised from the dead, dieth no more; death hath no more dominion over him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in that he died, he died to sin once: but in that he liveth, he liveth to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Likewise reckon ye also yourselves to be dead indeed to sin, but alive to God through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let not sin therefore reign in your mortal body, that ye should obey it in the lusts of it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Neither yield ye your members ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " instruments of unrighteousness to sin: but yield yourselves to God, as those that are alive from the dead, and your members ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " instruments of righteousness to God:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For sin shall not have dominion over you: for ye are not under the law, but under grace.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What then? shall we sin, because we are not under the law, but under grace? By no means.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Know ye not, that to whom ye yield yourselves servants in obedience, his servants ye are whom ye obey; whether of sin to death, or of obedience to righteousness?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But God be thanked, that ye were the servants of sin; but ye have obeyed from the heart that form of doctrine which was delivered you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Being then made free from sin, ye became the servants of righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I speak after the manner of men, because of the infirmity of your flesh: for as ye have yielded your members servants to uncleanness and to iniquity, to (",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": " work",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ") iniquity; even so now yield your members servants to righteousness, to (",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": " work",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ") holiness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For when ye were the servants of sin, ye were free from righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What fruit had ye then in those things of which ye are now ashamed? for the end of those things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now being made free from sin, and having become servants to God, ye have your fruit to holiness, and the end everlasting life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.6.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.6.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the wages of sin ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " death: but the gift of God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " eternal life, through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
